  "summary": "Renaissance rooms of wonders: unicorn horns, corals, automata and globes packed against carved walnut.",
  "description": "The Wunderkammer gathered the world into one room: narwhal \"unicorn\" horns, coral branches, celadon wares, Aztec featherwork, mechanical clocks, microcarvings on cherry pits, globes and scientific instruments, arranged in carved walnut cabinets and floor-to-ceiling painted stacks. Princes displayed dynastic reach; scholars debated nature's order across taxonomies that prefigured museums. Ole Worm's, Ferdinand II's Ambras and the Ashmole foundation map its arc into the first public museums — and its dense, allegorical wall-of-things look now reads as the ancestor of every collector's wall.",
